WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.451
The loop, step by step.

2
00:00:01.731 --> 00:00:07.789
Anthropic’s tool use course builds this up over several notebooks; here is the whole cycle in one place.

3
00:00:08.069 --> 00:00:08.709
One.

4
00:00:08.989 --> 00:00:12.104
You send a request with your messages and a tools list.

5
00:00:12.384 --> 00:00:13.109
Two.

6
00:00:13.389 --> 00:00:16.952
The model either answers directly or decides to use a tool.

7
00:00:17.232 --> 00:00:24.400
If it uses one, the response has a stop_reason of tool_use, and its content includes one or more tool_use blocks.

8
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:28.072
Each block has an id, a name, and an input object.

9
00:00:28.352 --> 00:00:34.475
The content may also include text, such as “Let me look that up,” and on current models, thinking blocks.

10
00:00:34.755 --> 00:00:35.501
Three.

11
00:00:35.781 --> 00:00:40.816
You append the assistant’s entire content to your message history, tool_use blocks included.

12
00:00:41.096 --> 00:00:41.821
Four.

13
00:00:42.101 --> 00:00:45.152
For each tool_use block, you run the matching function.

14
00:00:45.432 --> 00:00:46.200
Five.

15
00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:56.016
You send a new user message whose content is a list of tool_result blocks, each carrying the tool_use_id it answers and the result as content.

16
00:00:56.296 --> 00:00:57.043
Six.

17
00:00:57.323 --> 00:01:00.075
You call the API again with the longer history.

18
00:01:00.355 --> 00:01:07.075
The model reads the results and either requests more tools or finishes, in which case stop_reason is end_turn.

19
00:01:07.355 --> 00:01:14.693
Because the API is stateless (lesson 1), the history you resend is the only memory the model has of what it asked for.

20
00:01:14.973 --> 00:01:17.704
Two formatting rules from the docs trip people up.

21
00:01:17.984 --> 00:01:23.872
The user message with results must come immediately after the assistant message that requested them.

22
00:01:24.152 --> 00:01:29.656
And within that user message, the tool_result blocks must come first, before any text you add.

23
00:01:29.936 --> 00:01:31.685
Finally, put a ceiling on it.

24
00:01:31.965 --> 00:01:36.680
A model can keep asking for tools, and each round trip costs tokens and time.

25
00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:39.840
A maximum iteration count is cheap insurance.
